From: SaaiOS <os@saaios>
Subject: synaptics td4150: since53 0x42 immediately after 0x45, routing stays 0x04

since52 LIVE: switch_mode(BOOTLOADER) after HDL 0x1b selected 0x1f
because dispatch already stored IDENTIFY mode=0x02. SPI TX 1f 00 00,
retval=-62, no RX, IRQ=3, HDL_FAILED skip mod_resume. 0x1f is as deaf
as helper IDENTIFY. Samsung 0x42 is only selected from RomBoot 0x04.

Stock uses the 0x45 IDENTIFY as command completion without treating
host routing as already HDL. Next command is still 0x42 from 0x04.

since53: freeze routing_mode=0x04 during 0x45 IDENTIFY. After
write_message(0x45) returns, send CMD_ROMBOOT_RUN_BOOTLOADER_FIRMWARE
0x42 immediately in zeroflash_do_romboot_firmware_download (not the
delayed helper, not wait for 0x1b). Leftover 0x1b does not complete
the 0x42 waiter. No parallel HELP_SEND_REINIT until 0x42 settles.
No IDENTIFY as first post-0x45 command, no 0x1f, no ATTN drain.

diff -ruN a/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics/td4150/synaptics_tcm_core.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics/td4150/synaptics_tcm_core.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics/td4150/synaptics_tcm_core.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics/td4150/synaptics_tcm_core.c
@@
 	pr_info("SAaiOS_TOUCH_DBG: since52 switch_mode after 0x1b\n");
+	pr_info("SAaiOS_TOUCH_DBG: since53 probe\n");
+	pr_info("SAaiOS_TOUCH_DBG: since53 0x42 immediately after 0x45 routing stays 0x04\n");
 	pr_info("SAaiOS_TOUCH_DBG: probe enter\n");
